": false, "evidence": "rct", "ref_id": "NCT07231848"}, {"study_label": "Urolithin A (PK)", "outcome": "urolithin A kinetics in CSF", "arm": "mito", "direction": "unclear", "significant": false, "evidence": "observational", "ref_id": "NCT07517913"}], "gap_cells": [{"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NR, NMN, NADH, niacin)", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 6, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42669151", "40846977", "39173541", "42489969", "42774067", "NCT07344636"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NR)", "disease": "peripheral artery disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07782671"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (NMN/NR)", "disease": "age-related diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42068909"]}, {"intervention": "NAD+ precursors (boosters)", "disease": "musculoskeletal diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42727834"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42616901", "42432192"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "primary mitochondrial diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT07517913"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "frailty in older adults", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT06556706"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "unknown (bioavailability PK)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "rct", "refs": ["NCT07231848"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A", "disease": "Parkinson's disease", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42570712"]}, {"intervention": "urolithin A/B", "disease": "muscle health (skeletal muscle)", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42773997"]}, {"intervention": "NMN", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 2, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42573891", "42429864"]}, {"intervention": "Luteolin", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42013553"]}, {"intervention": "mitophagy (pharmacological, substrate-based, exercise)", "disease": "chronic heart failure", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "preclinical", "refs": ["42746169"]}, {"intervention": "nutritional optimization/exercise + emerging mito/anabolic/regenerative strategies", "disease": "skeletal muscle aging", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42769716"]}, {"intervention": "mitochondria-targeted natural-derived compounds", "disease": "cellular senescence", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "meta", "refs": ["42589194"]}, {"intervention": "AIRE (genetic predisposition analysis, diagnostic)", "disease": "autoimmune neurological diseases", "n_studies": 1, "top_evidence": "observational", "refs": ["NCT06941584"]}], "insights": ["No standard-of-care comparator appears in any record: all 63 plot markers are mito-side only, and no SOC benchmark (supportive care for primary mito diseases, idebenone for LHON, GDMT for CHF) is ever reported as an arm. LHON has no records at all, and four human trials carry no posted results, so they are coded pipeline-only with direction=unclear. (NCT07344636, NCT07782671, NCT06556706, NCT07231848)", "NAD+ precursors: the highest-tier human evidence is a 2026 meta-analysis (n=1599, primary mito diseases) showing significant gains in endurance (NMN high-dose SMD 1.02, 95% CI 0.43-1.60), quality of life (NMN SMD 0.56) and cognition (NADH SMD 1.50), but NULL on fatigue, sleep and neuromuscular strength - a mixed profile versus supportive care, with NAD+ elevation itself confirmed by a companion review. (42774067, 42489969)", "Chronic heart failure: all six studies are preclinical - urolithin A significantly improved diastolic function and remodeling (42616901) and favorably (ns) in a two-hit HFpEF model (42432192); NMN significantly improved fibrosis, cardiac function and ROS in vivo (42573891) and showed in-vitro cardioprotection (42429864); luteolin showed anti-injury/anti-ferroptosis effects (42013553). No agent has been tested head-to-head against GDMT. (42616901, 42432192, 42573891, 42429864, 42013553)", "Urolithin A is the most widely explored agent (CHF, PD, frailty, muscle, primary mito diseases) but every human dataset is PK or unreported: frailty RCT n=26 with no results (NCT06556706), Phase1 bioavailability PK (NCT07231848), CSF kinetics in primary mito diseases (NCT07517913); PD and muscle data are review/in-vitro only, so efficacy remains unproven. (NCT06556706, NCT07231848, NCT07517913, 42570712, 42773997)", "Negative/cautionary signals: NR aggravated erythrocyte maturation defects (worsening anemia) in the animal model (42669151); a single niacin case report (n=1, low confidence - uncontrolled, imprecise) showed meager clinical response without stopping disease progression (39173541); the NAD+ precursor meta-analysis was null on fatigue, sleep and strength (42774067); the AIRE diagnostic registry has no posted results (NCT06941584). (42669151, 39173541, 42774067, NCT06941584)"]}